# Adding a social provider

**Agent:** Ship **one PR** that completes every item in [PR checklist](#pr-checklist). Do not stop at backend-only unless the user explicitly scoped that. Extended prose and connect walkthrough: `web/src/content/docs/contribution-opportunities/add-provider.md`. Also follow **public-api-surface-sync**, **add-competitors** (competitor channel lists), **web-seo-pseo**, **agent-skill**, **source-project-neutrality**.

**Extensions Hub tag:** secret-admin only — no `listing_tags` SQL seeds.

## Connect family

| Family | Operator app? | User | Env / keys | Reference |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **OAuth** | Yes | Platform redirect | `config.integrations.*`, `infra/self-host/.env.example`, docker-compose row | threads, instagram-business, facebook |
| **Credentials** | No | API key in Add Channel | None — no `{PROVIDER}_*` placeholders | devto |
| **Browser extension** | No | Extension + signed-in on platform | `VITE_OPENQUOK_BROWSER_EXTENSION_ID`; extension `externally_connectable` | skool — `common/src/browser-extension/`, `extension/`, `web/src/lib/integrations/browser-extension/` |

## Identifier contract

One kebab-case slug everywhere: `provider.identifier`, DB `provider_identifier`, OAuth `/integration/oauth/{identifier}`, `getLaunchProviderConfig`, docs, `channels/catalog/platforms/{slug}.ts`, `/channels/{slug}`, tool routes, `/agents/{host}/{slug}`. Key `benchmarkSlots.ts` `PLATFORM_WINDOWS` by every slug the calculator passes.

## Backend

1. **`SocialProvider`** — `backend/integrations/providers/{id}/`: connect, `post`, `maxLength`; helpers for publish. **OAuth** / **credentials** (`customFields`, base64 JSON `code`) / **extension** (`isChromeExtension`, `extensionCookies`, `extensionToken`, `POST /integrations/extension-refresh`).
2. **Register** — `integrationManager.ts`.
3. **Config** — OAuth: `GlobalConfig`, `.env.development.example`, `infra/self-host/.env.example`, redirect URI. Credentials + extension: **no** operator OAuth env; `GET /public/social/:identifier` → **400** (dashboard connect only).
4. **Between-steps OAuth** — `pages()`, `fetchPageInformation()` when `isBetweenSteps` (Meta Page pattern).
5. **Publish settings** — resolver from `providerSettings` (flat CLI + nested buckets) + unit tests.
6. **`comment()`** — only if same-account follow-ups ship; else `postComment: 'NONE'` and no follow-up marketing.
7. **Tests** — connect, publish, follow-ups, cross-account plugs as applicable.
8. **Analytics** — if `analytics()` / `postAnalytics()` ship, add exact `provider.identifier` to `SUPPORTED_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER_IDENTIFIERS` in `web/src/data/social-providers.ts` (same PR). Skip when no analytics (e.g. extension-only Skool).
9. **Cross-account plugs** — `internalPlugCatalog()` + orchestrator handlers + `crossAccountPlugs` in settings when applicable; skip otherwise.

## Extensions Hub listing tag

`/secret-admin/catalog-manager/tags` → Name slugs to `provider.identifier`; description; tag groups (**Social platforms** + Videos/Photos/Text). No agent/MCP tags here. Live channels: tag when integration ships.

## Web (composer + connect)

1. **Launch config** — `{id}.provider.ts` + `providers/index.ts` (`postComment`, `comments`, validation).
2. **Preview** — `{id}Preview.svelte` + `ShowAllProviders` branch; `mediaStoragePaths` for blob classification; see [Post preview](#post-preview-when-composer-ships).
3. **Page picker** — `continue-provider/{id}.ts` when `isBetweenSteps`.
4. **Settings** — `{id}Settings.svelte` + `SettingsAccordion`; preview reads `effectivePreviewProviderSettings` from `previewChannel.id` (not `followUpTargetIntegrationId`).
5. **`social-providers.ts`** — display name, icon; analytics allow-list when applicable.
6. **Credentials** — `AddProvider` dialog; exclude from invite links; `IntegrationContinue` must not redirect to non-URL `state`.
7. **Extension** — `BrowserExtensionConnectDialog`, `browser-extension/*`, STORE/REMOVE refresh token; docs `installation/chrome-extension.md`.
8. **Connect docs** — `channels/connect.md`, `platforms/connect-rules.md`.

## Post preview (when composer ships)

Per-channel `{id}Preview.svelte` only (not `GeneralPreviewComponent` for shipped networks). Minimum: phone `max-w` frame, fixed aspect, correct `ImageSlider` variant for photos, `classify*PreviewMediaMode` + tests, wire `/p/[postId]`. References: `TiktokPreview.svelte`, `InstagramPreview.svelte`, `mediaDrop.ts`, `AddEditModal.svelte`. Image-heavy networks need letterbox — do not use full-width `object-cover` only.

## Follow-up comment preview (only when `comment()` ships)

Composer already passes `threadReplies` into `ShowAllProviders` → `{id}Preview`. Each follow-up-capable provider must **render** them (not only enable the Follow-up comments panel).

| Step | Action |
| --- | --- |
| `{id}Preview.svelte` | Accept `threadReplies` (+ `threadFinisher` if used); render below main post chrome |
| Reply UI | Use `PreviewScheduledSocialReplies` with a variant that matches the card (light vs dark). **Do not** use `variant="general"` on a light native card — theme `text-base-content` on `#FAFAFA`-style chrome hides reply text in dark composer UI. Add `variant="{id}"` in `PreviewScheduledSocialReplies.svelte` when needed (reference: `skool`, `instagram`, `threads`) |
| Wiring | `ShowAllProviders` branch must pass `{threadReplies}` (and `providerSettings` when settings affect preview) |
| Public link | `/p/[postId]` must pass the same `threadReplies` / settings as the composer (`AddEditModal` → `previewThreadRepliesVm`) |
| Bento / landing | Follow-up feature rows: mock one reply row (`threadReplies` + `hideProviderHelp` / `compactEditor` as peers do) — e.g. `BentoSkoolFollowUps.svelte`, `BentoThreadsMediaReplies.svelte` |
| Orchestrator | `orchestrator/providers/{id}.ts` `buildFollowUpCommentSettings` when comment publish needs root `providerSettings` (e.g. Skool group on reply payload) |

Smoke-test: add a follow-up row in the composer, focus preview on that channel, confirm reply **body text** is readable (not just the “Scheduled replies” heading).

## Follow-ups (only when `comment()` ships)

Update: `followUp.ts` (`channelSupportsFollowUpComments`, bucket); `PostDTO.ts` `replyChainBucketForProvider`; `orchestrator/providers/{id}.ts` scheduled publish hooks + `publishFollowUpReplies.ts` path; `SetGridTable.presenter` if needed; launch `postComment` / `comments`; `{bucket}.replies` in agent/CLI/docs; `threads-and-comments.md` row; complete [Follow-up comment preview](#follow-up-comment-preview-only-when-comment-ships) when marketed.

## Cross-account plugs (only when catalog ships them)

Update: `providerSettings.ts` bucket; `crossAccountPlugPreview.ts`; `AddEditModal` / `ShowAllProviders`; `{id}CrossAccountPlugsPreview.svelte`; orchestrator handlers; agent docs `{bucket}.crossAccountPlugs`. No shared generic plug preview component.

## Channel catalog & public SEO

**Catalog:** `channels/catalog/platforms/{slug}.ts` → `catalog/seeds.ts` (`PUBLIC_CHANNEL_LANDING_PAGES`). Fields: `slug`, `platformLabel`, `icon`, hero/meta, `featureSections` (≥3 comma-separated phrases per **title**; `bentoId` at go-live), FAQ, `docsPath`, `available`. Copy: problem-first, ASD-STE100 (short sentences, **you**). CTAs from `landing/hero-copy.ts` → `/pricing`. No new `+page` per slug.

**Go-live (`available: true`):** three feature bentos — `feature-bento.ts`, `BentoPublicChannelFeature.svelte`, `bento/minor-templates/{slug}/`; no generic `/landing/*.mp4`. Build-backlinks: `resolveSchedulePostComposerBentoId.ts` + `{slug}-post-editor` or `COMPOSER_BENTO_BY_CATALOG_SLUG` + test.

